  "claim_short": "A bounded finite branched-cover continuation of the reciprocal inverse gives a sharp answer. If the continuation has sheet degree d, then a boundary polynomial relation of degree at most r with E^1(Omega) coefficients is unique exactly when d>r (under full boundary compatibility for the converse). In particular, three inverse sheets imply the quadratic condition in Theorem 6.7(1), while one or two sheets produce an...",
